SEG = 'CAS'
CAT = 'cpbCases'
Q = [
('An RA shows: billed $250, allowed $160, paid $128, patient responsibility $32. The provider is in network. How much is written off as contractual?',
 '$90', ['$122', '$32', '$218'],
 "Contractual adjustment is billed minus allowed: $250 - $160 = $90. The $32 is the patient's share and is billed to the patient."),
('An RA for an in-network claim shows allowed $200, paid $160, coinsurance $40. What does the practice bill the patient?',
 '$40', ['$0', '$160', '$200'],
 'The patient owes the coinsurance shown as patient responsibility, $40; the rest of the charge above allowed is a contractual write-off.'),
("A Medicare claim: allowed $120, Part B deductible already met, Medicare pays 80%. What is the patient's coinsurance?",
 '$24', ['$96', '$12', '$30'],
 'With the deductible met, Medicare pays 80% ($96) and the 20% coinsurance is $24.'),
("A nonparticipating physician's nonpar fee schedule amount is $100. What is the most he can charge on an unassigned claim?",
 '$115', ['$95', '$100', '$120'],
 'The limiting charge is 115 percent of the nonparticipant fee schedule amount: $100 x 1.15 = $115.'),
('The participating fee schedule amount is $200. What is the nonparticipating fee schedule amount?',
 '$190', ['$180', '$200', '$230'],
 'Nonparticipating allowances are 95 percent of the fee schedule amount: $200 x 0.95 = $190.'),
("A primary plan allowed $300 and paid $240. The secondary plan pays the patient's remaining share. How much does the secondary pay at most?",
 '$60', ['$300', '$240', '$0'],
 "If the secondary covers the patient's share left after the primary, the most it pays is $300 - $240 = $60."),
('An A/R aging report shows $8,000 in the 0-30 column and $2,000 over 120 days. Which accounts need the most urgent follow-up?',
 'Those over 120 days', ['Those in 0-30 days', 'Those with insurance pending under 30 days', 'Those paid this week'],
 'Older balances are the least likely to be collected and may be near filing or appeal limits, so they come first.'),
('A claim denied as "not medically necessary" under an LCD. The note shows a covered diagnosis the coder missed. What is the best step?',
 'Add the missed code', ['Appeal with the LCD text only', 'Bill the patient under an ABN', 'Add modifier GZ, resubmit'],
 'When the record supports a covered diagnosis that was left off, correcting the claim fixes the coding error the LCD edit caught.'),
('A claim was denied for no prior authorization. The record shows the payer approved the service by phone before the visit. What should the appeal include?',
 "The approval's reference number", ['A new superbill for the visit', 'A signed ABN from the patient', "The member's plan ID number"],
 'Proof of the authorization the payer gave, such as its reference number and date, answers the stated denial reason.'),
('A surgeon bills an office visit 20 days after a 90-day surgery for a wound check. The claim is denied. Why?',
 'Global period follow-up', ['Missing modifier 25', 'Filed after the deadline', 'Missing the referring NPI'],
 'Related postoperative visits within the 90-day global period are included in the surgical payment.'),
("Day 20 after a 90-day surgery, the surgeon treats the patient's unrelated bronchitis. How should the visit be billed?",
 'E/M with modifier 24', ['E/M with modifier 25', 'E/M with no modifier', 'E/M with modifier 79'],
 'An unrelated visit in the postoperative period is reported with modifier 24 and a diagnosis showing it is unrelated.'),
('A dermatologist removes a lesion (10-day global) and also evaluates a new rash elsewhere in a separate workup. How is that visit billed?',
 'E/M with modifier 25', ['E/M with modifier 57', 'E/M with modifier 24', 'Not billable at all'],
 'A significant, separately identifiable E/M on the day of a minor procedure is billed with modifier 25.'),
('A Medicare remittance dated March 10 denies a claim. By about when must the redetermination be filed?',
 'Mid-July', ['Mid-April', 'Early May', 'The next March'],
 'Receipt is presumed 5 days after the notice date (March 15), and the request is due within 120 days, about July 13.'),
('A QIC decision is received June 1. The practice wants an ALJ hearing. By about when must it ask?',
 'Late July', ['Mid-June', 'Late September', 'December 1'],
 'An ALJ hearing request is due within 60 days of receipt of the reconsideration, so by about July 31.'),
('A Part B service was on February 3, 2026. When does the Medicare filing period end?',
 'February 3, 2027', ['December 31, 2026', 'December 31, 2027', 'August 3, 2026'],
 'Medicare claims are due within 12 months, or 1 calendar year, after the date of service.'),
('A physician claim lists a line with From date 03/02 and To date 03/30, for supplies. Which date sets timely filing?',
 'The From date', ['The To date', 'The date entered', 'The payment date'],
 'For professional claims with span dates, the line item From date is used to decide timeliness.'),
('A patient, 66, works for a 300-person employer and has its plan. The office sent the claim to Medicare first. What happens?',
 'Medicare denies it as secondary', ['Medicare pays and the plan reimburses', 'Medicare pays in full', 'The plan pays Medicare'],
 "With 20 or more employees, the group plan is primary; Medicare won't pay first and the claim must go to the plan."),
("A Medicare patient was hurt in a car crash. The auto insurer hasn't paid 150 days after the claim. No ORM is open. What may the office do?",
 'Bill Medicare conditionally', ['Bill the patient in full', 'Drop the claim', 'Resend to the auto insurer only'],
 'After the 120-day paid-promptly period with no ORM, Medicare may pay conditionally and recover later.'),
("A claim for a 90-day surgery was denied as a duplicate of last month's surgery. The second was an unrelated procedure. What fixes it?",
 'Resubmit with modifier 79', ['Resubmit with modifier 24', 'Resubmit with modifier 25', 'Appeal without changes'],
 'An unrelated procedure in the postoperative period is reported with modifier 79, which starts a new global period.'),
('An appeal letter for a medical necessity denial should include:',
 'The claim, reasons and records', ['A copy of the claim and RA', "The patient's signed statement", "The payer's fee schedule page"],
 'A strong appeal identifies the claim, explains why the decision is wrong and attaches the records that support it.'),
("A payer's policy covers a test once a year. A patient had it 10 months ago and wants it again. What should the Medicare biller do?",
 'Give an ABN before the test', ['Bill it with modifier GZ after', 'Change the diagnosis', 'Bill it as a different test'],
 'For a service over a frequency limit, the notifier issues an ABN before the service, stating the frequency limit as the reason.'),
('A Medicare patient refuses to sign a properly given ABN. What does CMS suggest?',
 'Note it; consider not treating', ['Treat and bill the patient', 'Treat and bill Medicare with GA', 'Give a new ABN next visit'],
 'If the patient refuses to sign, the notifier notes it and should consider not providing the service unless health and safety require it.'),
('An ABN was given for a test Medicare denied as not reasonable and necessary. Which modifier was on the claim?',
 'GA', ['GZ', 'GY', 'GX'],
 'GA shows a required ABN was issued and is on file; GZ means denial is expected and no ABN was given.'),
('A service is never a Medicare benefit and the office gave a voluntary notice. Which modifiers may go on the claim?',
 'GX and GY', ['GA and GZ', 'GA only', 'GK and GL'],
 'GY marks a statutorily excluded service and GX a voluntary notice; they may be used together.'),
('A claim shows 6 units of a code whose MUE is 4. No modifier or record explains it. What will likely happen?',
 'Excess units denied', ['All 6 units paid', 'Claim paid at 150%', 'Claim sent to the QIC'],
 'Units over the MUE are denied unless properly supported; MUEs stop payment for incorrect units of service.'),
('Two codes billed together hit an NCCI PTP edit. The services were on separate fingers. What may allow payment?',
 'XS, with supporting notes', ['Modifier 25 on both codes', 'Billing them on separate days', 'Dropping the second diagnosis'],
 "XS shows a separate structure; the record must support distinct sites, since a modifier can't be used just to bypass an edit."),
('An HMO member saw a specialist without a required referral and the claim was denied. Who may end up owing for the visit?',
 'Possibly the patient', ['The HMO, in full', 'Medicare, instead', 'The referring PCP'],
 "HMOs commonly require a referral; without one the service may not be covered under the member's plan terms."),
('An EPO member had a routine visit with an out-of-network doctor. How is it likely handled?',
 'Not covered by the plan', ['Covered at out-of-network rates', 'Covered in full', 'Sent to Medicaid'],
 'EPOs cover services only from in-network providers, except emergencies.'),
("A TRICARE For Life patient's claim went to TRICARE first. What should the biller do?",
 'Bill Medicare first', ['Bill the patient', 'Wait for TRICARE to pay', 'Bill Medigap'],
 'Medicare pays first for a TRICARE For Life beneficiary without employer coverage, then TRICARE pays second.'),
("A worker injured on the job asks the office to bill his health plan because his workers' comp claim is open. What is correct?",
 "Bill workers' compensation", ['Bill the health plan first', 'Bill the patient', 'Bill both plans equally'],
 "Workers' compensation is primary for job-related injuries; the employer's health plan is not billed first."),
("A payer pays $95 on a $100 allowed claim, then a second payer also pays $95. What is the practice's duty?",
 'Refund the duplicate', ['Hold it until the payer asks', "Credit the patient's account", 'Apply it to another claim'],
 'Money paid in error is returned to the payer that overpaid.'),
("A denial's remark says the provider wasn't enrolled on the date of service. What is the root cause?",
 'Enrollment gap', ['Wrong place of service', 'Missing modifier', 'Late patient copay'],
 'Claims from a provider not yet credentialed or enrolled with the payer are denied until enrollment covers the date.'),
('A claim was denied because coverage had ended before the date of service. What prevents this?',
 'Eligibility checks', ['Filing appeals sooner', 'Adding modifier 59', 'Adding a second diagnosis'],
 'A 270/271 eligibility check before the visit catches terminated coverage.'),
('A collection call is planned for a patient in another time zone. It is 7:30 a.m. there. What should the collector do?',
 'Wait until after 8 a.m. there', ['Call now; it is 9 a.m. at the office', 'Call and leave a voicemail', "Call the patient's employer"],
 "Inconvenient times are judged at the consumer's location: before 8 a.m. and after 9 p.m."),
("A patient tells the practice's collector that his employer bans personal calls at work. What applies?",
 'Stop calling him at work', ['Call only before noon', 'Call his supervisor instead', 'Call once a week'],
 'A collector may not communicate at the workplace when it knows the employer prohibits such communications.'),
("A patient's daughter calls and asks what her father still owes. He has not authorized her. What should the biller do?",
 'Decline to give account details', ['Give the balance only', 'Give the balance and the diagnosis', 'Mail the statement to her'],
 "Third-party communication about a debt is limited, and PHI disclosure to family needs the patient's permission or involvement."),
('A patient filed bankruptcy, and the practice still sends monthly statements for the old balance. What is wrong?',
 'It may break the stay', ['Nothing; statements are fine', 'It breaks the Stark Law', 'It breaks timely filing'],
 'The automatic stay bars acts to collect pre-petition claims against the debtor.'),
('An uninsured patient got a good faith estimate of $1,000 and a bill of $1,300. Can she use the dispute process?',
 "No, it's under $400 over", ['Yes, any amount over qualifies', 'Yes, at 10% over', 'Only if the provider agrees'],
 'The dispute process applies when the bill is at least $400 more than the estimate; $300 does not qualify.'),
('Medicare paid $80 after a patient paid $100 up front under an ABN. Allowed is $100. How much is refunded to the patient?',
 '$80', ['$100', '$20', '$0'],
 "The patient paid the full $100; Medicare's $80 makes the patient's share $20, so $80 is refunded."),
("A claim submitted on October 15 with no response. The payer's clean claim time is 30 days. When should the biller follow up?",
 'Around November 14', ['After 7 days', 'After 90 days', 'When the patient calls'],
 "Following up just after the payer's processing window passes catches lost or pended claims early."),
('A RA shows a CARC for a missing modifier. What does a CARC tell the biller?',
 'Why it was adjusted', ["The payer's mailing address", "The patient's plan ID", 'The allowed fee schedule'],
 'Claim adjustment reason codes on the 835 explain why a payment was adjusted or denied.'),
('A claim was paid, then the payer recouped it because another plan is primary. What should the biller do?',
 'Rebill in the right order', ['Appeal the recoupment', 'Bill the patient for it', 'Ask the payer to reverse it'],
 "When another plan is primary, the claim goes to it first and then to the secondary with the primary's payment information."),
('A provider bills an injection given by a nurse while the physician was out of the office for the day. What is the problem?',
 'No direct supervision', ['Missing modifier 25', 'No ABN was signed', 'Filed after the deadline'],
 'Incident-to billing in the office needs the physician present in the office suite and immediately available.'),
("A hospital patient's physician-employed nurse gives care during the inpatient stay. Can the physician bill it under Part B incident to?",
 'No, not as incident to', ['Yes, with modifier 25', 'Yes, under direct supervision', 'Yes, billed under Part B'],
 'There is no Part B incident-to coverage for physician-employed auxiliary staff during a hospital stay; it is covered only under the hospital benefit.'),
('Two staff members at the front desk write different insurance IDs for the same patient. What prevents denials from this?',
 'Card scan and eligibility check', ['Asking the patient at checkout', "Using the last claim's ID", "Calling the patient's employer"],
 "Scanning the insurance card and running an eligibility check makes the demographics on the claim match the payer's file."),
('A coder sees a claim with a symptom code and a note saying "suspected kidney stone" in the office. Is the claim right?',
 'Yes, the symptom is correct', ['No, code the kidney stone', 'No, add a rule-out code', 'No, leave the diagnosis blank'],
 'Outpatient guidelines code to the highest degree of certainty, so a suspected condition is reported by its symptoms.'),
("A payer's new policy limits a service, and the practice's claims for it start denying. What should billing do first?",
 'Read it, update edits', ['Appeal each denial as it comes', 'Add modifier 59 to those claims', 'Bill the patients directly'],
 'Payer payment policies change; the practice updates its edits and front-end rules to match the current policy.'),
('A practice finds it was paid twice by Medicare for the same claim. What does compliance require?',
 'Return it', ['Hold it until an audit', 'Apply it to old balances', 'Credit it to the patient'],
 'Responding to detected problems and returning money paid in error is part of an effective compliance program.'),
('A patient owes $1,200 and offers to pay $100 a month with no interest. Is this a Regulation Z credit plan?',
 'Yes, over four payments', ['No, there is no interest', "No, it's under $5,000", 'Yes, any plan is covered'],
 'Credit payable by written agreement in more than four installments makes a creditor under Regulation Z even with no finance charge.'),
('A dental office sends a claim on the 837 professional format. What will happen?',
 'Needs 837 dental', ['Paid normally', 'Needs the NCPDP format', 'Needs a UB-04 form'],
 'HIPAA names a separate 837 dental standard for dental claims.'),
('A Medicare beneficiary disputes a denial and gets a favorable redetermination. Who issues payment?',
 'The MAC', ['The QIC', 'The ALJ', "The patient's Medigap"],
 'The contractor effectuates decisions, including its own redeterminations and decisions made at later levels.'),
("A new patient by Medicare's rule: last seen by a same-specialty partner 4 years ago. Which visit type is billed?",
 'New patient visit', ['Established patient visit', 'Consultation', 'Preventive visit only'],
 'No professional service from the same-specialty group within 3 years makes the patient new for Medicare.'),
]
